# Image Captioning with CNN-LSTM

This project explores deep learning-based image captioning using the **Flickr8k** dataset. We combine a **Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)** for image feature extraction with a **Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM)** model for generating text captions. We also compare three decoding strategies: **Greedy Search**, **Beam Search**, and **Top-k Sampling**.

---

## Objective
To develop and evaluate an image captioning system that describes input images using natural language.

---

## Dataset: Flickr8k  
- 8,000 images of everyday scenes
- Each image has 5 human-written captions  
- Images resized and processed using the **Xception** CNN  
- Captions cleaned and tokenized (max length: 34 tokens)

---

## Model Architecture  
- **CNN Encoder**: Xception (2048D features)
- **Sequence Model**:
  - Embedding layer
  - LSTM with 256 units
  - Merged with CNN features
  - Dense output layer with softmax

---

## Decoding Strategies Compared
| Strategy     | Description                                 |
|--------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Greedy       | Selects the highest probability word each step |
| Beam Search  | Keeps top-k most probable sequences         |
| Top-k        | Samples from the top-k likely words at each step |

---

## BLEU Scores (on test set)

| Method      | BLEU-1 | BLEU-2 | BLEU-3 | BLEU-4 |
|-------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|
| Greedy      | 0.129  | 0.066  | 0.036  | 0.018  |
| Beam Search | 0.131  | 0.068  | 0.038  | 0.019  |
| Top-k       | 0.125  | 0.064  | 0.035  | 0.017  |

---

